[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Pinned stateless stop-grid qualification experiment

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QUAL-STOPGRID-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Bounded owned instrumentation of a pinned original analysis
STATEMENT: >>>
The qualification-only helper shall reproduce one io_ordering experiment using pinned SHA256 identities for the original physical deck/analysis bytes, retained engine manifest and existing native executable. It shall reject other input, original controls/resources, missing paths, existing output and excessive data before dispatch. It shall use the existing generated syntax catalog and public typed result contract, preserve every original physical/analysis byte, and insert only owned finite stop-time/run/resume/relative-write/quit commands. Native execution shall have a thirty-second limit; retained engine/native data shall have explicit point/byte bounds. Input/assembly identity changes shall invalidate the result.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: qualification-only StopGridQualification.cs and scripts/Run-StopGridPoc.cs. Reuses the existing generated ANTLR catalog, public ResultManifest reader and bounded ASCII RAW reader; no parser/dependency or production comparator change. Verification: StopGridQualificationTests unpinned-control/resource, malformed shape/unit/grid/value and native replay cases; existing output remains unchanged after refusal. Exactly101 retained engine rows and at most4096 native rows are admitted. Current original is CRLF byte-pinned; canonical-LF conversion is not the same admitted input.
<<<
